  "transition_and_terminal_rules": [
    "goat placement (both learner paths): board[pos] = 1, goats_placed += 1, phase = 1 once goats_placed >= 15 -> rules: gm | 1 << p, placed + 1 (placing while placed < 15)",
    "goat slide: dest = move_map[pos][dir]; board[pos] = 0, board[dest] = 1 -> rules: gm ^ 1 << p ^ 1 << N[p, d]",
    "tiger move: (dest, capture) from _tiger_moves keyed by (from, dir); capture removes _find_jumped_goat(from, dest) (checked above to be the goat the rules remove) and eaten += 1",
    "tigers win when eaten >= 6 right after the capture (both paths) -> rules: the 6th capture wins at once",
    "goats win when the tigers have no legal move on their turn (goat path: after the goat move; tiger path: after the goat reply) -> rules: a mover with no legal move loses",
    "tigers win when the goats have no legal move (tiger path: goat_random_action returns None) -> same rule; the goat-learner path has no such check (its mask is empty and any action is invalid)",
    "not in the solved game: the turn limit (MaxTimeout after max_turns) and RepeatTimeout (goat path, 4th occurrence of a board after the tiger reply); see README for how ply counts handle the turn limit",
    "observation -> position: placed = 15 in the movement phase, else goats on board + eaten, because the only writes (listed) keep goats_placed = goats on board + eaten during placement"
  ],
